{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-63920",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the index, we substitute our known values of ${a}_{1}$, $r$ and ${a}_{n}$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ 24 & =3\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{24}{3} & ={2}^{n-1} \\\\ 8 & ={2}^{n-1} \\\\ {2}^{3} & ={2}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n3=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=4\n$$\n\nWe can check this result by substituting $n=4$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{4-1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =24\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
